# Tests whose LEAKS=1 AddressSanitizer run (scripts/asan_check.sh) still reports leaks.
# Classification of the 131 (2026-11, after the tuple-ownership work): the leaks are whole-program ARC
# gaps in the std library code these programs exercise, not in the tests themselves -- List/Dict/Set
# values that escape their local (collections are raw, non-refcounted pointers freed only when sema
# proves a local never escapes), str/StringBuilder temporaries inside std parsers, class instances
# held by structures that are never torn down (std error objects, parsers), `str` boxes in
# Dict/Option/Result payloads, and tuples stored in collections or holding collections.
# A test must NOT be added here to hide a regression in a clean test: the clean set is
# tests/asan_clean.list and is gated in CI.  Remove a line when its test becomes leak-free.
